WEBVTT

00:24.149 --> 00:26.443
Don't look up without my permission.

00:27.068 --> 00:29.320
It makes me sick, brat.

00:30.864 --> 00:32.741
Then come on down.

00:32.824 --> 00:34.951
I'll look down on you.

02:16.219 --> 02:18.847
You look rather mad.

02:18.930 --> 02:22.809
Of course, I was killed by you.

02:22.892 --> 02:26.312
Have you forgotten
that I've healed your hands?

02:26.396 --> 02:29.149
But then you took my heart out,
didn't you?

02:31.401 --> 02:33.069
Is this hell?

02:33.153 --> 02:37.448
I don't like the idea that
I'm stuck with you even after I'm dead.

02:38.199 --> 02:39.951
But that's fine.

02:40.034 --> 02:41.327
I'll make you cry!

02:48.126 --> 02:50.211
Grit your teeth!

02:58.636 --> 03:01.180
He was aiming for the ground
from the beginning.

03:01.264 --> 03:02.515
You've been tricked!

03:02.599 --> 03:03.975
I did it!

03:05.018 --> 03:05.935
What?

03:06.603 --> 03:08.521
You're so boring.

03:12.859 --> 03:15.069
I thought I had that one in the bag.

03:16.279 --> 03:17.447
Darn it.

03:17.530 --> 03:19.115
This isn't hell.

03:19.949 --> 03:21.576
It's my Innate Domain.

03:21.659 --> 03:23.536
Innate Domain?

03:23.620 --> 03:25.705
I think Fushiguro mentioned this before.

03:25.788 --> 03:28.291
Think of this place
as somewhere inside my mind.

03:28.374 --> 03:31.669
-This means we’re not dead yet.
-What?

03:31.753 --> 03:34.047
As long as you agree to my terms,

03:34.130 --> 03:36.674
I'll heal your heart
and bring you back to life.

03:36.758 --> 03:38.384
You talk like you're so big.

03:38.468 --> 03:42.013
You've been putting on airs,
but you just don't want to die either!

03:42.597 --> 03:44.432
Circumstances have changed.

03:44.515 --> 03:45.725
Soon,

03:45.808 --> 03:48.519
you'll be able to witness
something interesting.

03:50.355 --> 03:52.232
I have two conditions.

03:52.315 --> 03:55.109
First, if I recite the chant "Enchain,"

03:55.193 --> 03:57.528
you must lend me your body for one minute.

03:57.612 --> 04:00.782
Second, you must forget
about this agreement.

04:00.865 --> 04:01.866
No way.

04:01.950 --> 04:04.827
I don't know what your motive is,
but it's too suspicious!

04:04.911 --> 04:07.205
After going through all that,
I finally understand.

04:07.288 --> 04:11.501
You're evil.
I'll never lend you my body again.

04:11.584 --> 04:16.798
Then I promise you, I won't kill
or hurt anyone within that one minute.

04:17.966 --> 04:18.967
This is so annoying.

04:19.050 --> 04:20.551
Who would believe that?

04:20.635 --> 04:23.680
There's no need to believe my words.

04:23.763 --> 04:25.390
This is a Binding Vow.

04:25.473 --> 04:27.016
In other words, an oath.

04:27.100 --> 04:29.644
If I don't keep my promise,
I'll be punished.

04:32.146 --> 04:34.565
If you take excess advantage
of our relationship,

04:34.649 --> 04:38.736
you'll have to pay the price.
You should have experienced it before.

04:39.570 --> 04:41.781
But nothing happened to you!

04:41.864 --> 04:42.907
What?

04:43.408 --> 04:46.995
Oh, I wanted to take over your body
that time, too.

04:47.078 --> 04:50.540
And you only did it because
that Jujutsu Sorcerer told you to do so.

04:53.710 --> 04:58.548
A Binding Vow with mutual interests
is one of the important creeds in sorcery.

05:01.009 --> 05:04.721
I see. Move aside.
I'll accept your conditions.

05:10.435 --> 05:13.396
I don't know what you're up to,

05:13.479 --> 05:16.357
but it's all for the sake of
coming back to life!

05:19.610 --> 05:21.487
As if I'll say that.

05:21.571 --> 05:23.781
Revive me with no conditions.

05:23.865 --> 05:26.576
I died because of you in the first place.

05:27.285 --> 05:28.953
Let's do this, then.

05:29.037 --> 05:32.582
Let's have a fight, and if you win,
I'll revive you unconditionally.

05:32.665 --> 05:35.877
If I win, I'll use
my Binding Vow to resurrect.

05:35.960 --> 05:37.962
Fine by me. I'll beat you to--

05:45.178 --> 05:46.429
I…

05:46.512 --> 05:48.514
I have a horrible personality, right?

05:48.598 --> 05:49.432
I know.

05:49.515 --> 05:51.684
I'm going to give you
a good slap later, Ijichi.

05:51.768 --> 05:53.644
A "good slap"?

05:54.312 --> 05:56.147
I'm not fit to be a teacher.

05:56.230 --> 05:59.734
But despite so,
why am I a teacher in a high school?

05:59.817 --> 06:01.110
Ask me.

06:01.819 --> 06:03.154
Why?

06:03.780 --> 06:05.573
I have a dream.

06:05.656 --> 06:07.575
A dream, you say?

06:07.658 --> 06:08.826
That's right.

06:08.910 --> 06:11.120
As you can see from what happened to Yuji,

06:11.204 --> 06:13.790
the higher-ups are the evil den
of the world of sorcery.

06:13.873 --> 06:17.335
They are all a bunch of selfish,
hereditary, arrogant,

06:17.418 --> 06:18.544
and ordinary fools.

06:19.045 --> 06:21.297
It's like rotten oranges on sale.

06:21.881 --> 06:25.176
I'm going to reset
this rotten sorcery world.

06:27.553 --> 06:30.640
It's easy to just kill the higher-ups.

06:30.723 --> 06:33.434
But a new group of people
will replace them eventually.

06:33.518 --> 06:35.144
It makes no difference.

06:35.228 --> 06:38.606
And no one would be
willing to join my cause.

06:39.607 --> 06:42.568
That's why I chose education.

06:43.069 --> 06:46.614
I want to nurture strong
and intelligent comrades.

06:47.782 --> 06:51.702
That is why I entrust my tasks
to my students at times.

06:51.786 --> 06:54.914
-They are my lashings of love.
-Weren't you just trying to skip work?

06:54.997 --> 06:56.582
All of them are outstanding.

06:57.166 --> 07:00.253
Especially the third-year Hakari
and second-year Okkotsu.

07:00.336 --> 07:03.089
They will grow to be as strong as me.

07:03.965 --> 07:06.175
Yuji was supposed to be
one of them as well.

07:09.679 --> 07:10.972
Hey, you two.

07:11.055 --> 07:12.056
-What?
-What?

07:12.140 --> 07:15.560
I'm about to start. Are you guys
going to watch from there?

07:17.103 --> 07:18.146
What?

07:19.188 --> 07:20.857
Wow, I'm naked.

07:20.940 --> 07:25.862
-Mr. Gojo, he's alive…
-Shut up, Ijichi!

07:25.945 --> 07:27.363
What a shame.

07:27.447 --> 07:29.449
Excuse me, but I'm embarrassed.

07:29.532 --> 07:30.366
Who are you?

07:30.450 --> 07:31.284
Yuji.

07:31.367 --> 07:32.201
What?

07:32.285 --> 07:33.119
GET DRESSED FIRST

07:33.202 --> 07:34.704
Welcome back.

07:35.955 --> 07:37.748
Hey! I'm back.

07:43.838 --> 07:46.924
I have to amend the report.

07:47.008 --> 07:48.593
No, you don't have to.

07:48.676 --> 07:49.594
What?

07:49.677 --> 07:51.345
We need some time for Yuji

07:51.429 --> 07:54.724
to gain strength
before he's targeted again.

07:54.807 --> 07:59.103
Shoko, please state in the report
that Yuji is dead for now.

07:59.187 --> 08:00.062
What?

08:00.146 --> 08:02.899
Then are you going to
hide Itadori forever?

08:02.982 --> 08:03.816
No.

08:03.900 --> 08:06.152
I'll let him return
before the exchange program.

08:06.235 --> 08:07.069
Why?

08:07.153 --> 08:08.529
The reason is simple.

08:09.322 --> 08:13.493
It's a sin to rob
the youth off of young people.

08:13.993 --> 08:16.245
Will everyone be shocked?

08:17.330 --> 08:19.165
It's the same for everyone.

08:25.463 --> 08:28.049
I'm going to quit my job now.

08:28.549 --> 08:31.093
I've been a responsible person
since I was young.

08:31.177 --> 08:35.139
I've saved up all my wages
to send my four stepsisters to school.

08:35.223 --> 08:37.808
But even I can't fight
against my survival instincts!

08:37.892 --> 08:40.144
If I get closer to that table, I'll die.

08:40.228 --> 08:42.146
Satoru Gojo.

08:42.230 --> 08:45.942
Is it impossible for us
to defeat him together?

08:46.025 --> 08:47.902
He'll either escape easily,

08:47.985 --> 08:50.571
or exorcise all of you, at worst.

08:51.072 --> 08:55.743
Instead of killing him, I would suggest
you find a way to seal him.

08:56.244 --> 08:58.538
Seal? With what?

08:59.163 --> 09:02.458
We can use a Special Grade Cursed Relic
known as the Prison Realm.

09:02.959 --> 09:05.336
Prison Realm?

09:05.419 --> 09:07.922
Table five doesn't order anything at all.

09:08.005 --> 09:11.467
Can anyone go and check it out?
There's only one person at that table.

09:11.551 --> 09:13.177
I'm sorry, Manager.

09:13.261 --> 09:15.429
-I'm going to quit my job!
-What?

09:15.930 --> 09:17.890
Hey, wait!

09:17.974 --> 09:21.352
Do you have that taboo object with you?

09:21.435 --> 09:24.105
What? The air-conditioner
is turned on, right?

09:24.814 --> 09:27.733
Jogo, don't get too excited.
It's getting hot in here.

09:28.985 --> 09:32.822
Sir, have you decided what to order--

09:38.828 --> 09:41.747
Don't create a scene.

09:41.831 --> 09:43.666
I'm sure this is fine.

09:46.294 --> 09:47.378
What?

09:56.512 --> 09:58.806
Luckily, I didn't choose
a high-class restaurant.

10:07.440 --> 10:12.028
Geto, how many fingers of Sukuna
are equal to my strength?

10:12.111 --> 10:15.448
As an overestimation,
around eight or nine?

10:16.490 --> 10:19.410
That's more than enough.
Hand me the Prison Realm.

10:19.493 --> 10:20.911
I'm adding it to my collection.

10:21.621 --> 10:23.873
In return…

10:24.665 --> 10:26.417
I'll kill Satoru Gojo.

10:27.418 --> 10:28.377
Help--

00:10:46.719 --> 00:10:51.724
When we arrived at the scene,
your son had already passed away.

00:10:52.558 --> 00:10:57.480
To be honest, I was hesitant
to save the people there.

00:10:58.105 --> 00:11:00.483
But my comrades said otherwise.

00:11:01.817 --> 00:11:03.527
Although we didn't make it,

00:11:04.111 --> 00:11:08.074
he insisted on bringing his body back
even after his death was confirmed.

00:11:10.326 --> 00:11:11.243
Please.

00:11:15.706 --> 00:11:16.582
TADASHI OKAZAKI

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.214
So I brought this back.

00:11:25.383 --> 00:11:27.051
TADASHI OKAZAKI

00:11:27.134 --> 00:11:28.803
I'm extremely sorry that

00:11:29.553 --> 00:11:31.430
I'm unable to save Tadashi.

00:11:34.141 --> 00:11:36.268
It's okay. Don't apologize.

00:11:36.352 --> 00:11:38.687
I'm the only one…

00:11:39.563 --> 00:11:42.233
who's sad about his death.

00:11:50.449 --> 00:11:52.827
You're too slow, Megumi.

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:53.869
Seaweed.

00:11:53.953 --> 00:11:55.037
What were you doing?

00:11:55.121 --> 00:11:56.372
It's not important.

00:11:57.915 --> 00:11:59.959
-Zenin.
-Yes?

00:12:00.459 --> 00:12:03.754
As a Jujutsu Sorcerer,
what kind of people do you want to save?

00:12:03.838 --> 00:12:04.880
What?

00:12:04.964 --> 00:12:08.467
I'm not interested in the people I save.

00:12:08.551 --> 00:12:09.844
I shouldn't have asked you.

00:12:09.927 --> 00:12:10.761
What?

00:12:10.845 --> 00:12:12.346
Fushiguro!

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:15.766
It's not the time for interviews!

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:21.230
I'm sick of my school uniform!
Let me buy some cute sportswear!

00:12:21.313 --> 00:12:23.732
Here it comes!

00:12:25.067 --> 00:12:27.027
What are they doing?

00:12:27.111 --> 00:12:29.155
-Falling practice.
-Mustard.

00:12:29.238 --> 00:12:31.240
You two are weak at fighting close-range.

00:12:31.323 --> 00:12:32.950
First of all…

00:12:34.785 --> 00:12:36.871
Try to take one point from us.

00:12:36.954 --> 00:12:38.539
Then we'll talk later.

00:12:39.623 --> 00:12:44.128
You should do a lot better than the others
in close-range combat, Yuji.

00:12:44.211 --> 00:12:45.963
What you need to learn now is

00:12:46.046 --> 00:12:47.798
to control your cursed energy,

00:12:47.882 --> 00:12:51.218
and some basic knowledge of curse.

00:12:51.302 --> 00:12:52.386
SMILING

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:53.721
What's wrong?

00:12:53.804 --> 00:12:55.848
Oh, I just thought that

00:12:55.931 --> 00:12:59.185
you're the best person
to train me, so I'm happy.

00:13:00.269 --> 00:13:03.230
I'm weak, and couldn't save anyone.

00:13:03.731 --> 00:13:06.400
Not only that, I nearly killed Fushiguro.

00:13:06.484 --> 00:13:10.571
I'm too ashamed to meet them.

00:13:11.739 --> 00:13:13.532
I want to be stronger.

00:13:15.743 --> 00:13:17.661
Teach me how to become the strongest.

00:13:21.707 --> 00:13:23.417
You've got a keen eye.

00:13:23.501 --> 00:13:26.795
But you said
you're the strongest, Mr. Gojo.

00:13:27.796 --> 00:13:31.008
All right. Please look at
the two juice cans over there.

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:36.305
Wow!

00:13:36.388 --> 00:13:40.059
I used cursed energy on this can
and cursed technique on this one.

00:13:40.142 --> 00:13:42.102
I see. I don't understand.

00:13:42.186 --> 00:13:44.063
Well, let's see.

00:13:44.146 --> 00:13:46.190
Let's compare cursed energy to electricity

00:13:46.273 --> 00:13:48.984
and cursed techniques
to electrical appliances.

00:13:49.068 --> 00:13:52.112
Electricity alone has limited uses, right?

00:13:52.613 --> 00:13:57.201
So electricity is charged into electrical
appliances for various purposes.

00:13:58.035 --> 00:14:00.955
This can was blasted by cursed energy

00:14:01.539 --> 00:14:03.415
and this can was twisted

00:14:03.499 --> 00:14:06.418
by infusing cursed energy
into a cursed technique.

00:14:07.628 --> 00:14:11.090
So that means I'm going to learn
a lot of cool techniques!

00:14:11.173 --> 00:14:13.425
No, you can't use curse.

00:14:14.009 --> 00:14:15.177
What?

00:14:15.261 --> 00:14:18.681
Let's not talk about basic Shikigami
or barrier techniques.

00:14:18.764 --> 00:14:20.474
Basically, cursed techniques are

00:14:20.558 --> 00:14:23.185
engraved on a Jujutsu Sorcerer's body
when he was born.

00:14:23.269 --> 00:14:25.688
-What?
-Thus, it's said that…

00:14:25.771 --> 00:14:29.108
80% of a Jujutsu Sorcerer's strength
comes from their innate talent.

00:14:31.151 --> 00:14:32.236
Are you okay?

00:14:32.319 --> 00:14:33.404
Well…

00:14:33.487 --> 00:14:37.575
I just thought I could have skills
like thunder, fire, or power bomb.

00:14:37.658 --> 00:14:40.494
You should be able to perform
a power bomb. Are you Onita?

00:14:41.495 --> 00:14:43.539
Forget about it then.

00:14:43.622 --> 00:14:47.501
I wanted to use Spirit Gun, Bankai,
Rasengan, or Dodonpa…

00:14:47.585 --> 00:14:50.087
-I thought I could use them…
-You just can't use it now.

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:53.424
One day, Sukuna's techniques
will be engraved into your body.

00:14:53.507 --> 00:14:56.510
-I wanted to use Kamehameha…
-Let's put aside what you can't do.

00:14:56.594 --> 00:14:58.220
I'll further develop your strengths

00:14:58.304 --> 00:15:00.347
and add cursed energy
to your martial arts.

00:15:00.431 --> 00:15:01.932
Ignore useless curse techniques.

00:15:02.016 --> 00:15:04.768
I'm scared of people like you
bulldozing through with basics!

00:15:04.852 --> 00:15:06.020
-What?
-As I said earlier,

00:15:06.103 --> 00:15:08.689
you have an impressive talent
for physical combat.

00:15:10.024 --> 00:15:12.735
But I'm already good at it!

00:15:12.818 --> 00:15:13.944
Get up, will you?

00:15:14.028 --> 00:15:16.530
At that time, I mastered
the trick without knowing.

00:15:20.576 --> 00:15:23.579
Well then, let's try it. Hit here.

00:15:23.662 --> 00:15:25.497
I bet you can't do it.

00:15:25.581 --> 00:15:27.541
I don't care if you get hurt.

00:15:27.625 --> 00:15:29.001
Just hurry up already.

00:15:33.297 --> 00:15:35.674
There's no cursed energy in it.

00:15:35.758 --> 00:15:36.926
Why?

00:15:37.009 --> 00:15:39.678
The source of cursed energy
is negative emotions.

00:15:39.762 --> 00:15:41.347
When you said "that time,"

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:43.974
you were full of anger and fear, right?

00:15:44.058 --> 00:15:48.938
Oh, do we have to be angry
in order to use cursed energy?

00:15:49.021 --> 00:15:52.608
Right, Fushiguro always looks like
he's about to snap.

00:15:52.691 --> 00:15:54.109
Divine Dog!

00:15:55.778 --> 00:15:56.737
You're wrong.

00:15:58.030 --> 00:15:59.073
What is it?

00:15:59.156 --> 00:16:01.533
-I feel annoyed all of a sudden.
-What?

00:16:01.617 --> 00:16:03.535
-No, it's not because of you.
-Salmon roe.

00:16:03.619 --> 00:16:06.538
The event is only a month and a half away.
Let's not waste time.

00:16:06.622 --> 00:16:08.958
Let's continue.
Try out this long one here.

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:13.754
This feels surprisingly nice to hold.

00:16:15.047 --> 00:16:17.299
Everyone undergoes training to draw

00:16:17.383 --> 00:16:19.468
cursed energy
from a single spark of emotion.

00:16:19.551 --> 00:16:22.137
When you're too emotional…

00:16:22.221 --> 00:16:23.222
I'm mad!

00:16:23.305 --> 00:16:25.683
…you should avoid wasting cursed energy.

00:16:27.351 --> 00:16:29.603
There are many ways to learn,

00:16:29.687 --> 00:16:32.272
but I'll let you do one
that's really tiring.

00:16:33.065 --> 00:16:34.233
What is it?

00:16:34.775 --> 00:16:36.527
Watching movies.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:38.028
Watching movies?

00:16:38.696 --> 00:16:39.530
That's right.

00:16:39.613 --> 00:16:43.158
It ranges from classic masterpieces
to C-class horror, even artistic French!

00:16:43.242 --> 00:16:45.661
As long as you're awake,
you have to keep watching it.

00:16:45.744 --> 00:16:47.746
Of course, it's not that easy.

00:16:50.499 --> 00:16:52.251
You have to watch it with this guy.

00:16:52.334 --> 00:16:54.586
What's with that disgustingly cute doll?

00:16:55.337 --> 00:16:56.630
Does this look cute?

00:16:56.714 --> 00:16:58.674
It's a Cursed Corpse
made by the principal.

00:16:58.757 --> 00:17:01.093
Oh, I knew it!
Looks like something he would make.

00:17:06.598 --> 00:17:09.268
So? I don't understand the point of it.

00:17:09.351 --> 00:17:11.770
Don't rush. It's starting soon.

00:17:14.189 --> 00:17:17.234
If that doesn't receive
a constant flow of cursed energy,

00:17:17.317 --> 00:17:19.570
it will wake up and attack you, like now.

00:17:19.653 --> 00:17:22.239
It hurts!

00:17:22.322 --> 00:17:23.574
Like I said,

00:17:23.657 --> 00:17:26.326
there are a variety of movies.

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:28.912
It will make you anxious, angry, excited.

00:17:28.996 --> 00:17:31.498
Some will make you cry, laugh,
or just plain disgusted!

00:17:32.624 --> 00:17:34.585
First, try to sit through an entire movie

00:17:34.668 --> 00:17:37.004
without waking the doll up
and hurting yourself.

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:40.799
This training helps you maintain
a constant flow of cursed energy

00:17:40.883 --> 00:17:42.426
regardless of what you're feeling.

00:17:42.509 --> 00:17:44.470
You can't emit too much
or too little power.

00:17:49.683 --> 00:17:53.937
I've set the required amount of energy
to the bare minimum you are able to emit.

00:17:54.021 --> 00:17:58.484
But the required flow
will increase slowly, so don't slack off.

00:17:58.567 --> 00:18:01.320
I can't slack off even if I want to.

00:18:01.403 --> 00:18:04.239
Which one do you want to watch first?
I recommend this one.

00:18:04.323 --> 00:18:07.076
The heroine's a nasty girl,
but she gets a gaudy death.

00:18:07.159 --> 00:18:08.786
That's a huge spoiler.

00:18:08.869 --> 00:18:11.246
Let's see.
We should watch an action movie--

00:18:12.831 --> 00:18:14.541
Jeez!

00:18:14.625 --> 00:18:17.711
Come on! You have to keep the flow stable
even if you're irritated.

00:18:18.879 --> 00:18:21.298
How to carry a Cursed Tool?

00:18:21.381 --> 00:18:24.760
I agree to using special weapons
to enhance close-range combat.

00:18:24.843 --> 00:18:28.555
But I would like to keep myself
hands-free to use techniques.

00:18:28.639 --> 00:18:31.266
It also uses up time to sheathe a knife.

00:18:32.142 --> 00:18:35.813
You carry multiple Cursed Tools,
right, Zenin?

00:18:35.896 --> 00:18:37.189
How do you manage them?

00:18:37.731 --> 00:18:38.899
I let Panda carry them.

00:18:38.982 --> 00:18:41.235
Once again, I shouldn't have asked her.

00:18:41.819 --> 00:18:45.864
There are Jujutsu Sorcerers that
tame familiars to store weapons for them.

00:18:45.948 --> 00:18:48.575
That's impossible to learn.
It's a rare ability, too.

00:18:48.659 --> 00:18:50.953
It also takes time to tame it.

00:18:51.036 --> 00:18:52.663
Let me know if you find one.

00:18:52.746 --> 00:18:54.456
A year's supply of Karpas.

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:57.334
I don't understand. Back then…

00:19:00.337 --> 00:19:01.755
Why did you escape?

00:19:03.006 --> 00:19:04.925
It's a waste of your talent.

00:19:05.008 --> 00:19:08.929
He thinks that I have the potential to
defeat that Special Grade Cursed Spirit.

00:19:09.721 --> 00:19:11.932
Is that what he meant?

00:19:17.146 --> 00:19:18.230
Tuna…

00:19:18.313 --> 00:19:19.148
What?

00:19:19.231 --> 00:19:20.065
What's wrong?

00:19:21.275 --> 00:19:22.568
Zenin.

00:19:23.652 --> 00:19:25.571
I think I might be able to do something.

00:19:30.534 --> 00:19:31.577
Urahara!

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:33.537
Where's Urahara? Is it underground?

00:19:35.455 --> 00:19:39.543
Red and blue wire, which one should I cut?

00:19:41.378 --> 00:19:44.798
There was a garbage collection point
near my old address.

00:19:44.882 --> 00:19:47.634
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:19:47.718 --> 00:19:50.804
We throw plastic waste into the red bin,
combustibles into the blue.

00:19:50.888 --> 00:19:53.974
I thought to myself,
"Shouldn't it be the other way round?"

00:19:54.057 --> 00:19:56.310
That's right, it's usually red.

00:19:57.728 --> 00:19:59.313
I'll believe you.

00:20:15.829 --> 00:20:17.956
Don't do it when I'm drinking cola!

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.208
Don't drink, then.

00:20:19.291 --> 00:20:22.002
You always have snacks and cola
while watching movies!

00:20:22.085 --> 00:20:23.337
You're right.

00:20:24.796 --> 00:20:28.717
Well then, I have something to do,
so keep working hard.

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:31.136
Can I really grow stronger with this?

00:20:34.223 --> 00:20:35.432
Oh, right.

00:20:36.016 --> 00:20:38.393
Have you talked to Sukuna
while you're dead?

00:20:38.894 --> 00:20:40.020
Talk?

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:45.734
Did he offer you any conditions
or contracts to fix your heart?

00:20:45.817 --> 00:20:47.236
Yes…

00:20:47.319 --> 00:20:49.446
I think he said something.

00:20:50.405 --> 00:20:52.699
I can't really remember.

00:20:53.533 --> 00:20:54.868
Is that so?

00:20:59.706 --> 00:21:02.668
We still have time before
our appointment with the principal.

00:21:02.751 --> 00:21:04.378
Do you want to take a short detour?

00:21:04.461 --> 00:21:07.631
No, I should be early once in a while.

00:21:11.927 --> 00:21:12.803
Stop the car.

00:21:12.886 --> 00:21:14.638
What? Right here?

00:21:15.222 --> 00:21:17.140
-You can go first.
-What?

00:21:17.224 --> 00:21:19.434
Is this some kind of test?

00:21:19.518 --> 00:21:21.853
Are you going to beat me up if I leave?

00:21:21.937 --> 00:21:23.689
Who do you think I am?

00:21:23.772 --> 00:21:25.440
Okay, I'll leave then.

00:21:33.657 --> 00:21:34.700
Well then…

00:21:42.541 --> 00:21:45.252
Who are you?

00:23:16.593 --> 00:23:18.553
-Juju Stroll!
-Juju Stroll!

00:23:20.222 --> 00:23:23.058
"Satoru Gojo's Go-Go-Gojo!"

00:23:23.141 --> 00:23:27.562
Today, we're at my alma mater,
Tokyo Prefectural Jujutsu High School.

00:23:27.646 --> 00:23:28.563
What?

00:23:28.647 --> 00:23:30.273
And here's a student in trouble.

00:23:30.357 --> 00:23:31.650
Is he a freshman?

00:23:31.733 --> 00:23:34.820
He can't seem to extract cursed energy.
Let's give him some advice.

00:23:35.403 --> 00:23:38.406
You're walking down a narrow road.

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.867
There's a row of male students
in front of you.

00:23:40.951 --> 00:23:42.702
They didn't notice you.

00:23:42.786 --> 00:23:44.371
You feel like killing them, right?

00:23:44.454 --> 00:23:45.997
-So--
-Shut up.
